{
  "_comment": [
    "THE RECIPE FIXTURE for the mock API — item 5.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS",
    "-------------------",
    "Live has ZERO published recipes: the `recipe_published` view has no",
    "rows, so every hub and every recipe page on the real site renders its",
    "EMPTY state. That empty state is the deliverable today, and the",
    "mock must reproduce it faithfully — an empty list, not a 404.",
    "",
    "But a build that can only ever produce the empty state cannot prove",
    "the POPULATED path: that the recipe list renders, that the filter",
    "island works, that the recipe page shows its ingredients, its",
    "sentences and its confidence. Those are the parts that break when",
    "the shape drifts.",
    "",
    "So the mock serves the recipe routes from THIS file, and it serves",
    "THEM EMPTY by default — matching live — with the recipes below",
    "reachable ONLY when the build asks for them explicitly.",
    "",
    "THE SWITCH",
    "----------",
    "The `X-Gustale-Fixture: recipes` request header turns the populated",
    "fixture on. Without it the mock returns the EMPTY shape (total 0),",
    "which is exactly what live returns.",
    "",
    "So a plain build is the empty state, and a build with the header is",
    "the populated state. Both are exercised, and neither is a lie: the",
    "empty shape is what the API really returns today.",
    "",
    "THE SHAPES",
    "---------",
    "Every field here mirrors apps/api/src/routes/recipes.ts exactly —",
    "the `shapeRecipe()` output for a list row, and the detail response",
    "for one recipe. When the API's shape changes, this file changes",
    "with it."
  ],
